    {
      "id": "sticky-wf1-main",
      "name": "Workflow Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1600,
        1264
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 268,
        "content": "## Monitor and throttle CPU spikes on a Hostinger VPS with AI triage\n\nMonitors a Hostinger VPS every 15 minutes for CPU spikes. When CPU exceeds the configured threshold, it collects the process list via SSH, asks an AI model to analyse the cause, and emails you a report with a reply-to-kill option.\n\nTwo parallel branches: (1) detection/analysis/notify loop, and (2) kill-approval listener (IMAP) that waits for an email reply containing 'KILL', takes a snapshot, then terminates flagged processes.\n\n**Requires:** Hostinger API, SSH Password, IMAP, SMTP, and Anthropic credentials."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-wf1-step1",
      "name": "Stage 1: Schedule & Config",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1824,
        2032
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 340,
        "height": 154,
        "content": "**Stage 1 — Schedule & Config**\n\nFires every 15 minutes. The Config node sets vpsId, SSH host, email, and detection thresholds. Edit the Config node values before activating."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-wf1-step2",
      "name": "Stage 2: Metrics & Detection",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2272,
        2032
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 500,
        "height": 138,
        "content": "**Stage 2 — Metrics & Detection**\n\nFetches 2-hour CPU/traffic metrics from Hostinger API. Code node computes whether CPU has exceeded the threshold and whether traffic is anomalous."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-wf1-step3",
      "name": "Stage 3: Process List & AI",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2976,
        1968
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 154,
        "content": "**Stage 3 — Process List & AI Analysis**\n\nRuns 'ps aux --sort=-%cpu' via SSH. Formats top processes into an HTML table. Sends raw output to the Anthropic model to identify the likely cause and give a remediation recommendation."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-wf1-step4",
      "name": "Stage 4: Traffic & Non-Traffic Paths",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4032,
        1792
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 580,
        "height": 250,
        "content": "**Stage 4a — Traffic-Driven Path**\n\nIf a traffic anomaly is detected, finds or creates a lockdown firewall allowing only ports 22/80/443 and activates it on the VPS. Sends a lockdown notification email.\n\n**Stage 4b — Non-Traffic Path**\n\nLogs the case to /var/log/n8n-cpu-guard.log and emails a process report with reply-to-kill instructions."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-wf1-kill",
      "name": "Kill Approval Branch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1840,
        2528
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 158,
        "content": "**Kill Approval Branch (IMAP listener)**\n\nRuns in parallel. Watches for email replies containing 'KILL' in the body and a CPU case ID in the subject. Reads the case from the SSH log, takes a VPS snapshot, waits 45 s, then terminates the flagged PIDs via SSH."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-wf1-security",
      "name": "Security Warning",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1600,
        1552
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "**Security & Cost Warnings**\n\n- The kill command runs as the SSH user — ensure this account has minimum necessary privileges.\n- The firewall lockdown blocks all non-SSH/HTTP/HTTPS traffic; legitimate services may be disrupted.\n- Anthropic API calls cost tokens per invocation (every 15 min during a spike). Monitor usage.\n- A VPS snapshot is taken on every kill approval and consumes storage quota.\n- IMAP polling interval determines kill-approval latency."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-wf1-community",
      "name": "Community Node Disclaimer",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1600,
        1760
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 780,
        "height": 130,
        "content": "**Community Node — Self-Hosted n8n Required**\n\nThis workflow uses n8n-nodes-hostinger-api, a community-maintained node not available on n8n Cloud. Install it on a self-hosted instance via: Settings > Community Nodes > Install > n8n-nodes-hostinger-api."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
